Aim
To write a Python program to perform various operations on a tuple, such as finding its length, maximum, minimum, sum, count, index, accessing elements, reversing, and slicing

Algorithm
Start the program.
Create a tuple t = (10, 20, 30, 40).
Display the original tuple.
Find and display the length of the tuple using len().
Find and display the maximum and minimum values using max() and min().
Calculate and display the sum of all elements using sum().
Count the occurrences of 20 using count().
Find the index of 30 using index().
Display the element at index 0.
Reverse the tuple using slicing [::-1].
Display the sliced tuple using [1:4].
Stop the program.

code
t = (10, 20, 30, 40)

print("Original tuple:", t)

print("Length:", len(t))

print("Maximum value:", max(t))

print("Minimum value:", min(t))

print("Sum:", sum(t))

print("Count of 20;", t.count(20))

print("Index of 30:", t.index(30))

print("Element at index 0:", t[0])

print("Tuple in reverse:", t[::-1])

print("Tuple in slicing:", t[1:4]) 


output 
